      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Produce one original square production atlas for a first-grade math game set in a neighborhood badge-exhibit workshop. Keep a strict two-by-two equal grid with no printed labels, no grid lines, and no content crossing the cell boundaries. Overall style is fine paper texture, matte gouache, clean cut-paper shapes, deep pine green and warm cream with apricot and persimmon accents, soft daylight. No text, letters, numbers, logos, watermark, captions, countable piles or math diagrams. Top-left cell is a full-bleed warm scene of a tidy community exhibit check-in desk with two closed wooden trays on the countertop, quiet shelves behind, friendly and uncluttered, center-framed. Top-right cell is a different full-bleed quiet workshop with pale empty floor in the middle, low distant cabinets along the edges, subdued background to let moving game elements stand out. Bottom-left cell is transparent, with two separate small mint-green toy pushcarts facing right, left the resting frame and right an active rolling frame of the same recognizable cart, generous clear transparent margins. Bottom-right cell is transparent, with three clean separate isolated icons across a single row, left a small pine-green tabletop ball launcher angled upward, center a compact apricot marble with a paper sheen, right a persimmon-and-pine rosette reward sticker. No drop shadow or opaque paper background behind any bottom asset. Precise quantities and math text will be added as code outside this atlas."
